      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day by prescription, and the single dose is also twice the usual 800 mg ceiling. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Some common options are:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), which is typical for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), for inflammatory conditions.\n\nIf you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm the indication and your clinical rationale. I would also suggest checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
